1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,500
Cinderella

2
00:00:05,490 --> 00:00:12,070
Cinderella's Sister

3
00:00:39,640 --> 00:00:43,680
Cinderella's Sister

4
00:00:50,590 --> 00:00:53,660
Do you even like Hyo Seon's dad?

5
00:00:53,660 --> 00:00:55,290
Why are you asking me something like that?

6
00:00:55,290 --> 00:00:58,640
Tell me you at least like him a little!

7
00:00:58,640 --> 00:01:01,610
If you say he's not just someone you can take a lot from,

8
00:01:01,610 --> 00:01:04,550
but someone you actually like,

9
00:01:04,550 --> 00:01:06,680
then I'll forgive you.

10
00:01:06,680 --> 00:01:09,210
Why are you causing such a fuss?

11
00:01:09,210 --> 00:01:10,760
I like him, why?

12
00:01:10,760 --> 00:01:14,660
I like him. I like him because he has a lot I can take from him! Why?

13
00:01:21,960 --> 00:01:26,350
Don't smile at people you can't get anything from.

14
00:01:26,350 --> 00:01:30,070
Don't trust anyone who just smiles your way, either.

15
00:01:30,070 --> 00:01:32,870
Do you know what it means to live?

16
00:01:32,890 --> 00:01:37,160
No matter how hard to study and show off that brain of yours,

17
00:01:37,160 --> 00:01:43,040
you will never know how hard it is to get by.

18
00:02:09,380 --> 00:02:11,150
Episode 7

19
00:03:00,390 --> 00:03:02,080
Excuse me...

20
00:03:04,540 --> 00:03:06,570
Excuse me!

21
00:03:41,400 --> 00:03:46,940
I'm just upset it's been confirmed with what she said.

22
00:03:47,700 --> 00:03:50,400
It's not like I didn't know before.

23
00:03:51,820 --> 00:03:53,280
What?

24
00:03:56,100 --> 00:03:59,690
Did you think I wouldn't know

25
00:03:59,690 --> 00:04:02,860
how your mother felt about me?

26
00:04:13,210 --> 00:04:20,470
I need to go back to the factory. Take a taxi back home with Mom.

27
00:04:24,770 --> 00:04:32,780
Don't tell your mom that I heard you two talking.

28
00:04:33,480 --> 00:04:40,580
If she knows, then she'll try hard to redeem herself.

29
00:04:44,140 --> 00:04:47,700
I don't want to see her trying too hard.

30
00:05:22,590 --> 00:05:25,840
When Eun Jo first became family,

31
00:05:26,600 --> 00:05:31,400
I was really happy I had an older sister

32
00:05:33,250 --> 00:05:36,060
and I really liked Eun Jo,

33
00:05:36,920 --> 00:05:39,590
even though she kept pushing me away.

34
00:05:40,400 --> 00:05:45,190
Whenever Eun Jo made conversation with me,

35
00:05:45,190 --> 00:05:48,240
I liked it so much I laughed all day.

36
00:05:48,240 --> 00:05:51,110
Even if she cursed at me, I was happy.

37
00:05:52,300 --> 00:05:56,990
How could she

38
00:05:57,760 --> 00:06:01,070
How can she do this to me?

39
00:06:02,080 --> 00:06:07,750
How can she make my worrying about her seem so pitiful?

40
00:06:07,750 --> 00:06:09,660
Don't cry.

41
00:06:14,180 --> 00:06:16,140
Cut it out.

42
00:06:25,200 --> 00:06:28,570
Stolen? Who's stealing from you?

43
00:06:28,570 --> 00:06:33,030
If you don't want to get it stolen, then pay attention and protect what's yours!

44
00:06:33,030 --> 00:06:34,530
Why...

45
00:06:35,490 --> 00:06:37,430
are you yelling at me?

46
00:06:37,430 --> 00:06:40,620
Why? Can I not yell at you?

47
00:06:40,620 --> 00:06:43,300
Is no one allowed to be angry at you?

48
00:06:43,300 --> 00:06:47,170
Do we have to be proud of everything you do?

49
00:06:48,320 --> 00:06:53,050
- Oppa...
- We accept it, laugh, and clap for you. Is that all we should do?

50
00:06:53,050 --> 00:06:55,350
Why are you so immature?

51
00:06:56,470 --> 00:07:01,490
What have you made yourself, with your own efforts, without leaning on anyone else?

52
00:07:01,490 --> 00:07:05,780
What have you done with your own hands and own strength?

53
00:07:05,780 --> 00:07:08,140
Did Eun Jo take it from you?

54
00:07:08,140 --> 00:07:12,020
How could she take it from you when you've never earned anything?

55
00:07:13,570 --> 00:07:16,540
What is it? Why are you looking?

56
00:07:16,540 --> 00:07:19,370
Why are you looking at me like that? Do you feel wronged?

57
00:07:19,370 --> 00:07:22,100
Are you angry I'm not taking your side?

58
00:07:22,100 --> 00:07:24,320
I'm not yours, you punk!

59
00:07:25,320 --> 00:07:29,820
I dare you to cry. If you do, I won't let you be.

60
00:07:33,880 --> 00:07:39,530
Oppa ... Don't do that. I'm afraid.

61
00:07:39,530 --> 00:07:41,600
I said stop it!

62
00:07:42,790 --> 00:07:44,080
Oppa, why are you being like this?

63
00:07:44,080 --> 00:07:46,090
Stop

64
00:07:48,470 --> 00:07:54,070
Your enemy is not Eun Jo. You should make your own things.

65
00:07:54,070 --> 00:07:59,190
And the things you make, you should protect.

66
00:07:59,190 --> 00:08:04,740
If you don't do that, even if things get taken from you, you can't say anything about it. Understand?

67
00:08:04,740 --> 00:08:07,380
You'll have nothing to say even if it's taken from you!

68
00:08:11,530 --> 00:08:17,920
Don't rely on me either. Even if you rely on me, I won't accept it.

69
00:08:21,860 --> 00:08:26,560
In the time you spend whining like this, you should clean one more jar.

70
00:08:29,210 --> 00:08:31,340
Hurry up and grow into an adult.

71
00:08:34,420 --> 00:08:36,160
Hurry.

72
00:08:55,940 --> 00:08:57,630
Get in.

73
00:09:00,550 --> 00:09:02,370
Aren't you getting in?

74
00:09:24,050 --> 00:09:27,540
Wow, you're good at this!

75
00:09:27,540 --> 00:09:29,970
Yes, I'm good.

76
00:09:29,970 --> 00:09:32,780
Should we scout him to the kitchen?

77
00:09:32,780 --> 00:09:37,870
That'll be hard to do. I'm quite expensive, so you'll need to double the wage.

78
00:09:40,120 --> 00:09:44,440
Goodness. You should head out now. I heard you're going on a picnic today?

79
00:09:44,440 --> 00:09:47,900
I'll follow them after I'm done with this. I'll do it.

80
00:10:37,630 --> 00:10:38,840
Hello?

81
00:10:38,840 --> 00:10:43,350
Is this the place you make Daeseong rice wine or Daeseong fake rice wine?

82
00:10:43,350 --> 00:10:47,770
- What?
- You're all dead! Where are you?

83
00:10:47,770 --> 00:10:51,300
How dare you joke around with food? Let me speak to your CEO!

84
00:10:51,300 --> 00:10:56,090
Hello? Who are you? What do you mean, joke around?

85
00:10:56,090 --> 00:10:58,500
Stop saying hello this and hello that.

86
00:10:58,500 --> 00:11:02,070
Stay right there! I'm heading over!

87
00:11:13,470 --> 00:11:15,580
Are you here alone?

88
00:11:17,830 --> 00:11:19,510
Who are you?

89
00:11:20,530 --> 00:11:24,940
The kitchen granny's told me to give this to your eldest daughter.

90
00:11:26,020 --> 00:11:28,090
She didn't come with me.

91
00:11:55,150 --> 00:11:57,720
I told you to go in and rest.

92
00:12:16,380 --> 00:12:21,500
You need to rest. Head home.

93
00:12:23,070 --> 00:12:27,560
How... can you do that?

94
00:12:30,010 --> 00:12:34,700
Even though you know... how?

95
00:12:44,460 --> 00:12:46,750
Know what?

96
00:12:47,640 --> 00:12:49,860
After knowing that she's by my side only

97
00:12:49,860 --> 00:12:53,360
because she has things to take from me?

98
00:12:55,420 --> 00:12:57,090
Yes.

99
00:12:58,590 --> 00:13:00,560
That's alright.

100
00:13:03,710 --> 00:13:08,960
Why? Why is that alright?

101
00:13:08,960 --> 00:13:14,430
How can that be okay? Until when was it okay?

102
00:13:14,430 --> 00:13:21,320
If you knew, how could you let Mom... and me?

103
00:13:22,540 --> 00:13:26,300
I take pity on your mother,

104
00:13:26,300 --> 00:13:28,580
who can't help but think the way she does.

105
00:13:31,940 --> 00:13:35,040
When you first came to me,

106
00:13:35,040 --> 00:13:37,270
and spoke whatever came to your mind,

107
00:13:37,270 --> 00:13:40,280
as you had learned from your mother,

108
00:13:40,280 --> 00:13:44,120
I thought how nice it would be if I could go into your past,

109
00:13:44,120 --> 00:13:46,700
before you met me, and protect you.

110
00:13:46,700 --> 00:13:52,790
I took pity on you enough to think those thoughts.

111
00:13:56,160 --> 00:14:01,340
It doesn't matter, because I love your mother.

112
00:14:03,450 --> 00:14:06,050
Getting my things taken from me

113
00:14:06,050 --> 00:14:12,530
is much better than you or your mother not being by my side.

114
00:14:13,910 --> 00:14:15,940
I'm telling you the truth.

115
00:14:20,020 --> 00:14:24,240
Goodness... This won't do.

116
00:14:24,240 --> 00:14:27,710
You can't cry like this, you're supposed to be resting.

117
00:14:27,710 --> 00:14:32,260
Come on, let's go home. Let's rest today.

118
00:14:32,260 --> 00:14:37,940
Do you want to go follow the others out on their picnic?

119
00:14:37,940 --> 00:14:42,330
We can go see the flowers. Shall we take Gi Hoon?

120
00:14:44,560 --> 00:14:51,070
What can I do?

121
00:14:54,630 --> 00:14:57,020
Don't abandon me.

122
00:15:01,660 --> 00:15:05,660
If you do that, then I'll be grateful.

123
00:15:10,770 --> 00:15:11,760
Let's go!

124
00:15:11,760 --> 00:15:15,110
♫  In the depth of my heart ♫

125
00:15:15,110 --> 00:15:21,670
♫ When loneliness comes again ♫

126
00:15:21,670 --> 00:15:27,000
♫  I also don't know again what you intend ♫

127
00:15:27,000 --> 00:15:32,840
♫  Without saying anything, smile again ♫

128
00:15:32,840 --> 00:15:36,560
♫  More than saying you loved me ♫

129
00:15:36,560 --> 00:15:42,440
♫  while you silently look at me ♫

130
00:15:42,440 --> 00:15:48,440
♫  I said I liked you so much and loved you ♫

131
00:15:48,440 --> 00:15:52,610
♫  My love, will you run to me? ♫

132
00:15:52,610 --> 00:15:58,430
Head it!
♫  I too unconsciously am waiting for you. ♫

133
00:15:58,430 --> 00:16:06,490
♫  I too unconsciously am waiting for you ♫

134
00:16:06,490 --> 00:16:08,130
Give it to me.

135
00:16:09,360 --> 00:16:15,150
♫ I am going to love you this way ♫

136
00:16:18,260 --> 00:16:19,890
Unknown Caller

137
00:16:21,720 --> 00:16:27,070
- Hello?
- Where are you? I'm at the office alone, without trying to rely on anyone.

138
00:16:27,070 --> 00:16:31,750
I'm trying to do something, but I don't know how to.

139
00:16:35,270 --> 00:16:41,130
Try it. I said try it! Is this rice wine or poop?

140
00:16:41,130 --> 00:16:44,350
Don't you know what happens when you mess around with food?

141
00:16:44,350 --> 00:16:47,530
Tell your president to come out! Isn't he here?

142
00:16:47,530 --> 00:16:49,900
Why?

143
00:16:49,900 --> 00:16:52,900
What's wrong with the taste?

144
00:16:52,910 --> 00:16:57,500
What would we say with you, miss? Go call the president!

145
00:16:57,500 --> 00:17:02,250
Does it taste weird? How is it weird?

146
00:17:02,250 --> 00:17:04,580
Give me that.

147
00:17:08,780 --> 00:17:13,490
- It's spoiled.
- How could you sell spoiled alcohol?

148
00:17:19,190 --> 00:17:21,890
This is spoiled, too!

149
00:17:21,890 --> 00:17:23,490
Tell the president to come out!

150
00:17:23,490 --> 00:17:28,400
You should have a conscience when trying to do business. Is he in here?

151
00:17:30,250 --> 00:17:32,910
But misters!

152
00:17:34,400 --> 00:17:37,620
This isn't our rice wine.

153
00:17:37,620 --> 00:17:42,680
The bottles are our bottles, but the alcohol inside isn't ours.

154
00:17:42,680 --> 00:17:46,680
Goodness... What do you mean that isn't alcohol from here?

155
00:17:46,680 --> 00:17:50,310
These days, we don't have any leftover stock because our rice wine sells well,

156
00:17:50,310 --> 00:17:56,630
but when we used to have leftover stock, we used to make vinegar with it.

157
00:17:56,630 --> 00:17:58,490
It wouldn't become so spoiled to the point of undrinkable,

158
00:17:58,490 --> 00:18:01,470
just because its expiration date passes.

159
00:18:01,470 --> 00:18:07,180
This definitely isn't our alcohol. I know it well.

160
00:18:07,180 --> 00:18:10,260
Do you want to make a bet with me?

161
00:18:10,260 --> 00:18:13,710
If you lose the bet, what do you want to give up?

162
00:18:36,490 --> 00:18:38,830
Has something like this happened before?

163
00:18:38,830 --> 00:18:44,020
No. Hurry up. Hyo Seon is alone.

164
00:18:44,020 --> 00:18:47,500
I know. I'm going quickly.

165
00:19:01,210 --> 00:19:03,140
Cheers!

166
00:19:03,140 --> 00:19:04,980
Drink up. Drink, drink!

167
00:19:04,980 --> 00:19:10,870
Have another glass. Isn't it delicious?

168
00:19:16,630 --> 00:19:22,080
Ever since I was born, I ws given my mother's milk half the time,

169
00:19:22,080 --> 00:19:24,970
and Daeseong's rice wine the other half the time.

170
00:19:24,970 --> 00:19:27,550
That's how I grew up.

171
00:19:27,550 --> 00:19:31,300
There's no way I wouldn't know the taste of our alcohol.

172
00:19:31,300 --> 00:19:34,410
The vinegar you make with our rice wine tastes...

173
00:19:34,410 --> 00:19:38,420
Um... Gosh.

174
00:19:38,420 --> 00:19:42,880
I can't explain it with words. Why aren't they coming?

175
00:19:42,890 --> 00:19:46,610
I asked granny to bring us some vinegar.

176
00:19:46,610 --> 00:19:52,690
What about we take another shot and sing a few more songs while we wait?

177
00:19:52,690 --> 00:19:57,240
Sounds good! Have another shot!

178
00:19:57,240 --> 00:19:59,770
Here, here!
One, two, three, four-

179
00:20:33,560 --> 00:20:36,160
Dad,

180
00:20:36,160 --> 00:20:41,590
This isn't our alcohol. It's not our alcohol, but it's in our bottles.

181
00:21:05,840 --> 00:21:12,310
The rice wine tastes great!

182
00:21:12,310 --> 00:21:13,980
Drink up!

183
00:21:13,980 --> 00:21:18,770
Hello. I'm Goo Dae Seong, president of Dae Seong True Winemakers.

184
00:21:18,770 --> 00:21:23,650
Oh, you're the president!

185
00:21:23,650 --> 00:21:26,370
It's spoiled.

186
00:21:26,370 --> 00:21:30,220
I told you it was spoiled. You don't believe me, do you?

187
00:21:30,220 --> 00:21:34,040
You had to check it for yourself because you couldn't believe me?

188
00:21:34,040 --> 00:21:38,640
Who mixed a different rice wine with ours? Where did they get this?

189
00:21:41,830 --> 00:21:44,050
Jumbo Supermarket (a supermarket is actually a small corner convenience store with produce) in Bangbae-dong.

190
00:21:45,320 --> 00:21:47,180
Bangbae-dong?

191
00:21:50,370 --> 00:21:51,940
What I'm saying is...

192
00:21:51,970 --> 00:21:54,450
You need to understand what I'm saying.

193
00:21:54,450 --> 00:21:58,210
No matter who asks, say you don't know.

194
00:21:58,210 --> 00:22:00,990
How much money did you get from me?

195
00:22:01,010 --> 00:22:05,040
Since you got that, you need to stay quiet.

196
00:22:06,820 --> 00:22:10,520
Goodness, this little punk has organs the size of the pea!

197
00:22:10,540 --> 00:22:15,540
What do you mean, my organs are the size of a pea? Have you forgotten where I'm from?

198
00:22:17,040 --> 00:22:18,980
Shut up, you punk.

199
00:22:25,180 --> 00:22:28,420
Daeseong Company, which illegally distributed barrels of makgeolli (rice wine), was finally caught.

200
00:22:28,500 --> 00:22:31,400
Detection of high levels of Sodium Saccharin discovered.

201
00:22:31,400 --> 00:22:34,300
As a result of the inspection to Daeseong Conpany which illegally distributed barrels of makgeolli,

202
00:22:34,300 --> 00:22:37,800
Sodium Saccharin, an additive prohibited in making makgeolli, was detected by Korea Food and Drug Administration.

203
00:22:37,810 --> 00:22:40,710
The expiration date of our wine is

204
00:22:40,710 --> 00:22:43,220
shorter compared to other brands of wine.

205
00:22:43,220 --> 00:22:47,810
Other brands of rice wine use additional preservatives

206
00:22:47,810 --> 00:22:50,750
or high-temperature sterilization to extend the shelf-life of their wine.

207
00:22:50,750 --> 00:22:53,370
But, we don't use that method.

208
00:22:53,370 --> 00:22:55,650
A day before the labelled expiration date,

209
00:22:55,650 --> 00:22:59,000
we collect any unsold remaining product.

210
00:22:59,000 --> 00:23:02,450
Because we have recently not had anything left unsold, there was no reason to collect expired product.

211
00:23:02,450 --> 00:23:05,470
Are you advertising your wine right in front of the police right now?

212
00:23:05,470 --> 00:23:07,120
Do you want us to buy more?

213
00:23:07,120 --> 00:23:08,870
There is no evidence anywhere in our production process to show

214
00:23:08,870 --> 00:23:12,630
that we added prohibited additive Sodium Saccharin in our makgeolli (rice wine).

215
00:23:12,630 --> 00:23:14,100
You already investigated.

216
00:23:14,100 --> 00:23:17,170
However, thereis Sodium Saccharin found in the spoilt wine in question.

217
00:23:17,170 --> 00:23:22,120
That is something someone malicious has done to slander our alcohol.

218
00:23:25,020 --> 00:23:26,250
This is definitely not a problem with the manufacturing process,

219
00:23:26,250 --> 00:23:29,230
but a problem with the distribution process for sure.

220
00:23:29,230 --> 00:23:31,200
Please investigate the distribution process.

221
00:23:31,200 --> 00:23:34,010
We will try our best to cooperate in the investigation without hiding anything

222
00:23:34,010 --> 00:23:35,630
We never said we wouldn't cooperate.

223
00:23:35,630 --> 00:23:38,930
Isn't it your duty to finish the investigation as soon as possible?

224
00:23:38,930 --> 00:23:41,130
We have been repeating ourselves for a few days already.

225
00:23:41,130 --> 00:23:44,120
In the meantime, it's just not only the spoilt wine in question that is being distributed in our region...

226
00:23:44,120 --> 00:23:48,640
Returns are coming in from other parts of the country and we have lost all of our orders.

227
00:23:59,670 --> 00:24:01,760
Don't get agitated.

228
00:24:01,760 --> 00:24:03,670
It will be fine.

229
00:24:11,210 --> 00:24:16,560
What should we do?

230
00:24:20,070 --> 00:24:22,050
Oh, right.

231
00:24:23,980 --> 00:24:30,330
You've told me not to rely on anyone right?

232
00:24:32,350 --> 00:24:38,400
Is there nothing that I can do at this time?

233
00:24:42,680 --> 00:24:48,120
Can I not even ask this?

234
00:24:50,140 --> 00:24:54,880
Is asking a question relying on you as well?

235
00:24:59,670 --> 00:25:01,660
I understand.

236
00:25:03,400 --> 00:25:05,560
I won't ask anymore.

237
00:25:08,580 --> 00:25:11,840
It's a relief that this happened before we expanded our facilities.

238
00:25:11,840 --> 00:25:16,460
If we had expanded, we would have produced more and more would be returned.

239
00:25:18,130 --> 00:25:20,130
It can be solved,

240
00:25:22,000 --> 00:25:24,020
So don't worry about it.

241
00:25:26,830 --> 00:25:32,630
Can you say it to me one more time, Oppa?

242
00:25:36,710 --> 00:25:42,650
Just now, it's just like when you said the moon is square, right?

243
00:25:46,170 --> 00:25:48,760
You said it can be solved

244
00:25:48,760 --> 00:25:51,530
and asked me not to worry.

245
00:25:52,640 --> 00:25:55,570
I really felt like it can be solved...

246
00:25:55,570 --> 00:25:58,140
So I don't have to worry.

247
00:26:22,990 --> 00:26:27,690
If you entrusted it to me then you should have waited. It's not even a child's play.

248
00:26:27,690 --> 00:26:30,130
What kind of recklessness is this?

249
00:26:30,160 --> 00:26:33,760
Do you think you can get Dae Seong True Winemakers through this method?

250
00:26:34,910 --> 00:26:37,470
It's not me.

251
00:26:37,470 --> 00:26:39,060
It's not?

252
00:26:39,060 --> 00:26:43,960
Do I look like someone who would play games like this?

253
00:26:43,960 --> 00:26:48,180
Then is it Gi Jeong?

254
00:26:50,250 --> 00:26:56,680
You really don't know me or Gi Jeong at all, do you?

255
00:26:56,680 --> 00:26:59,090
It's not me or Gi Jeong.

256
00:27:01,440 --> 00:27:04,720
The blow to their reputation will be huge.

257
00:27:04,720 --> 00:27:08,830
Both Gi Jeong and I are likely thinking the same thing.

258
00:27:08,830 --> 00:27:14,380
We are thankful for help to someone we don't know.

259
00:27:15,590 --> 00:27:21,150
Don't even try to pull something at this opportunity. Wait.

260
00:27:22,750 --> 00:27:26,470
Just what are you intending to do?

261
00:27:26,470 --> 00:27:30,510
I'm going to take over Daeseong before Gi Jeong can,

262
00:27:30,510 --> 00:27:33,540
and bloody his nose in the process.

263
00:27:35,220 --> 00:27:40,390
I'm not going to make Daeseong fail due to its ruined reputation.

264
00:27:40,390 --> 00:27:45,020
I'm going to take it. I don't want something that's failed.

265
00:27:45,020 --> 00:27:50,060
I'm going to develop it and take it. That's best for you, too.

266
00:27:56,500 --> 00:28:00,100
Is that so? Father and Gi Hoon?

267
00:28:00,100 --> 00:28:01,680
Yes.

268
00:28:04,000 --> 00:28:09,320
Gi Hoon, by any chance didn't he enter Dae Seong True Winemakers already?

269
00:28:09,320 --> 00:28:10,920
Yes.

270
00:28:10,920 --> 00:28:12,690
What is father planning?

271
00:28:12,690 --> 00:28:14,630
Since Gi Hoon has returned,

272
00:28:14,630 --> 00:28:17,660
but hasn't stayed properly motivated,

273
00:28:17,660 --> 00:28:19,970
I think he told him to just remain there.

274
00:28:19,970 --> 00:28:22,210
Father's minion.

275
00:28:23,090 --> 00:28:26,750
You don't like the term "minion", do you?

276
00:28:29,350 --> 00:28:33,770
Well, I guess, I must use it.

277
00:28:36,700 --> 00:28:40,630
As father's minion, you assisted him for a long time.

278
00:28:40,630 --> 00:28:43,270
Can't you let your feelings go?

279
00:28:44,420 --> 00:28:49,910
You think my father does not know that you and I are talking?

280
00:28:50,650 --> 00:28:54,340
He knows what Gi Hoon is planning, but is pretending not to know.

281
00:28:54,340 --> 00:28:56,450
That's the kind of person he is.

282
00:28:58,060 --> 00:29:01,920
Father can read your intentions like a book.

283
00:29:01,920 --> 00:29:05,700
Why can't you read his?

284
00:29:07,320 --> 00:29:09,440
Try reading it.

285
00:29:11,000 --> 00:29:12,400
I understand.

286
00:29:12,400 --> 00:29:14,410
You can leave now.

287
00:29:15,910 --> 00:29:17,460
Yes, sir.

288
00:29:54,230 --> 00:29:56,090
Are they failing?

289
00:29:57,750 --> 00:30:00,770
- What?
- Is this business going to fail?

290
00:30:01,850 --> 00:30:05,780
What's going to happen? Can we get anything from it?

291
00:30:05,780 --> 00:30:08,370
If the factory fails, can we not even get the company?

292
00:30:08,370 --> 00:30:11,430
What about this house? Can we take the house?

293
00:30:16,570 --> 00:30:19,110
You have to focus.

294
00:30:19,110 --> 00:30:21,270
Before everything goes to shambles,

295
00:30:21,270 --> 00:30:26,020
secretly prepare at least a house.

296
00:30:26,020 --> 00:30:29,340
Make everything you can make yours on paper.

297
00:30:29,340 --> 00:30:31,080
Stop.

298
00:30:32,150 --> 00:30:38,230
Mom, please. Please stop.

299
00:30:38,230 --> 00:30:41,510
What do you mean, please stop?

300
00:30:45,870 --> 00:30:50,740
They're not going to fail. Even if they do,

301
00:30:50,740 --> 00:30:53,030
they'll be lots for you to take.

302
00:30:53,030 --> 00:30:55,770
Very very much.

303
00:30:55,770 --> 00:30:58,900
You'll die from being so stuffed you can't breathe,

304
00:30:58,900 --> 00:31:01,710
but not because you starved.

305
00:31:03,250 --> 00:31:04,890
Really?

306
00:31:07,970 --> 00:31:09,820
Okay then.

307
00:31:50,980 --> 00:31:53,310
How many envelopes of money did I give you?

308
00:31:53,310 --> 00:31:57,380
Since you accepted that, you have to stay quiet, too.

309
00:33:34,660 --> 00:33:38,870
♫ In the colors... (In Spanish}

310
00:33:38,870 --> 00:33:46,980
♫ In the colors is the rainbow that we see shining? (In Spanish}

311
00:33:48,780 --> 00:33:58,710
♫ And that is why I love the great loves of many colors(In Spanish}

312
00:33:58,710 --> 00:34:09,160
♫ And that is why I love the great loves of many colors(In Spanish}

313
00:34:26,890 --> 00:34:34,200
♫ In the solicitude which wakes me up ♫

314
00:34:34,200 --> 00:34:41,610
♫when I wake up from an exhausted sleep♫

315
00:34:41,610 --> 00:34:47,990
♫because I still remember you smiling♫

316
00:34:47,990 --> 00:34:56,430
♫I'm secretly smiling♫

317
00:34:56,430 --> 00:34:59,650
♫Love leaves again this way♫

318
00:34:59,650 --> 00:35:01,330
Excuse me.

319
00:35:03,720 --> 00:35:08,950
♫When the beautiful season arrives ♫

320
00:35:08,950 --> 00:35:12,110
- Excuse me.
- What?

321
00:35:14,030 --> 00:35:16,600
Excuse me, the thing is that...

322
00:35:20,080 --> 00:35:23,330
It's nothing. Salute.

323
00:35:23,330 --> 00:35:30,630
♫I am living day after day ♫

324
00:35:30,630 --> 00:35:39,580
♫In your name when tears appear, ah♫

325
00:35:39,580 --> 00:35:47,030
♫I can't bear it so I can't laugh♫

326
00:35:47,030 --> 00:35:57,700
♫I'll call out your name again♫

327
00:36:14,060 --> 00:36:15,910
Turn off the light.

328
00:36:36,190 --> 00:36:40,550
Let's give this a try. Between us.

329
00:36:42,190 --> 00:36:44,260
What are you talking about?

330
00:36:44,290 --> 00:36:47,430
I won't let you have everything.

331
00:36:51,810 --> 00:36:57,460
There was a time when I wanted to be like you.

332
00:36:59,090 --> 00:37:05,620
You did well in your studies, you were smart, and haughty.

333
00:37:07,770 --> 00:37:14,130
And also... your I-don't-need-anyone attitude.

334
00:37:16,240 --> 00:37:23,610
Even if no one is looking, that look of arrogance as if it's nothing.

335
00:37:26,230 --> 00:37:30,970
There was a time when I thought you were so cool.

336
00:37:32,900 --> 00:37:40,920
But then you always splashed cold water on whatever I longed for.

337
00:37:42,440 --> 00:37:47,740
Let's give this a try. I'm not sure what I'm supposed to do yet,

338
00:37:50,080 --> 00:37:52,090
but I said let's give it a try.

339
00:39:25,660 --> 00:39:28,490
- Open it.
- Yes.

340
00:39:54,600 --> 00:39:57,220
I had no idea this was what he was doing.

341
00:39:57,980 --> 00:40:03,460
He said just to have a taste, so I did only taste it.

342
00:40:03,460 --> 00:40:08,960
Looks like they mixed the drinks here. President, over there.

343
00:40:15,590 --> 00:40:21,980
Dae Seong True Wine Makers makgeolli

344
00:40:28,100 --> 00:40:35,350
♫ Whatever it is you wanted, I did everything for you
Fun Fun - Joo Joo Club

345
00:40:35,350 --> 00:40:40,400
♫ Today for me

346
00:40:40,400 --> 00:40:42,580
I'm telling you this...

347
00:40:42,580 --> 00:40:48,370
I had bought land that was abandoned you know? It'll soon be developed.

348
00:40:48,370 --> 00:40:54,910
If we just do the presentation then this will double!

349
00:40:54,910 --> 00:41:02,410
Girls! Girls! Just trust me! I will buy you a diamond ring that's as big as an egg.

350
00:41:17,670 --> 00:41:21,150
I'm... against it.

351
00:41:22,400 --> 00:41:26,360
He's my mom's little brother.

352
00:41:26,360 --> 00:41:31,470
We can't call the police to catch my uncle who has ran away.

353
00:41:31,470 --> 00:41:34,620
The production in the factory has completely stopped.

354
00:41:34,620 --> 00:41:37,660
If we are to get rid of this wronged incident and run the factories,

355
00:41:37,660 --> 00:41:43,460
He's my uncle! He has nowhere else to go.

356
00:41:45,280 --> 00:41:47,890
Where and what on earth is he doing?

357
00:41:47,890 --> 00:41:52,930
We don't have time. You'd better make a decision on this.

358
00:41:53,790 --> 00:41:59,870
I... while also protecting Hyo Seon's uncle

359
00:41:59,870 --> 00:42:03,400
we need to think of a way to save the factory.

360
00:42:03,410 --> 00:42:05,280
How much time...

361
00:42:06,540 --> 00:42:09,670
How much time is needed to recover the broken trust

362
00:42:09,670 --> 00:42:13,080
and if it will even be recovered, that we don't know.

363
00:42:13,080 --> 00:42:18,250
Slowly... we can go slow.

364
00:42:18,250 --> 00:42:21,970
I can't do that. Are we in a circumstance where we can do that?

365
00:42:21,970 --> 00:42:24,940
We want to have a TV ad but even if our budget was at it's best--

366
00:42:24,940 --> 00:42:29,570
That's enough. Let's take it easy.

367
00:42:29,570 --> 00:42:32,520
We can start again slowly.

368
00:42:56,930 --> 00:43:01,870
Let's think of a way to redeem ourselves after we've posted an apology notice in the newspapers.

369
00:43:01,870 --> 00:43:06,460
Are you crazy? Why would we release an apology when we've done nothing wrong?

370
00:43:06,460 --> 00:43:10,070
It is the fault of the corporation for not being able to control its employees.

371
00:43:10,070 --> 00:43:12,830
I can't believe he did it alone.

372
00:43:12,830 --> 00:43:16,090
I'm sure there are others involved.

373
00:43:16,090 --> 00:43:18,820
If no one else will, I will report it to the police.

374
00:43:22,270 --> 00:43:24,520
Try to understand the president's wishes.

375
00:43:24,520 --> 00:43:26,390
Stop acting like you're better than everyone.

376
00:43:26,390 --> 00:43:29,340
Daeseong Company can recover quickly.

377
00:43:29,340 --> 00:43:33,520
Because the taste of our wine is better than that of others,

378
00:43:33,520 --> 00:43:37,490
people are already thinking that it's a good thing Dae Seong's rice wine won't be getting too much attention,

379
00:43:37,490 --> 00:43:40,650
and we're getting calls that we've never gotten before.

380
00:43:41,360 --> 00:43:44,880
Are you talking about the single call we got last week?

381
00:43:46,000 --> 00:43:48,770
Do you think that was really an interest call?

382
00:43:48,770 --> 00:43:54,300
Shouldn't you be producing more? Aren't you going to run your factories? Can we run them for you?

383
00:43:54,300 --> 00:44:00,920
There are already thieves lining up to swallow Daeseung Company whole, you naive idiot.

384
00:44:00,920 --> 00:44:04,000
At my insistence we spent lavish amounts of money on a commercial,

385
00:44:04,000 --> 00:44:08,640
but now I want to die because of everything that got canceled thanks to this incident. Do you know that?

386
00:44:22,270 --> 00:44:28,140
Wait. Talk to me for a bit. What does that mean? Are others going to take over?

387
00:44:28,140 --> 00:44:29,520
Move.

388
00:44:29,520 --> 00:44:31,880
Tell me a bit more in detail!

389
00:44:32,890 --> 00:44:34,940
Let go of her, then speak.

390
00:44:36,670 --> 00:44:39,860
Where is that? Can't you find out?

391
00:44:39,860 --> 00:44:43,160
Why does it matter to you? We're not going to sell it.

392
00:44:47,350 --> 00:44:49,120
Move!

393
00:44:51,870 --> 00:44:56,770
No, no. We won't meet you. If you want to meet about that, then there's no reason for us to meet.

394
00:44:56,770 --> 00:44:58,960
No, no. Please don't come.

395
00:44:58,960 --> 00:45:01,970
Daeseung Company will not fail because of something like this.

396
00:45:01,970 --> 00:45:04,600
We will not sell it to anyone!

397
00:45:07,250 --> 00:45:08,880
Gosh...

398
00:45:29,920 --> 00:45:32,100
Dad...

399
00:45:37,120 --> 00:45:38,800
Dad?

400
00:45:40,560 --> 00:45:43,520
You haven't shaved, have you?

401
00:45:43,520 --> 00:45:45,570
Why are you being like this?

402
00:45:49,080 --> 00:45:54,550
I want to be someone whom you find helpful

403
00:45:55,860 --> 00:45:59,240
and you can rely on.

404
00:46:02,680 --> 00:46:05,910
I really want to do that,

405
00:46:09,130 --> 00:46:13,410
but I'm nothing, right?

406
00:46:14,910 --> 00:46:17,250
Why would you say that?

407
00:46:19,420 --> 00:46:23,490
Right now, I may be nothing,

408
00:46:24,510 --> 00:46:29,590
but I'll slowly become your strength, Dad.

409
00:46:32,960 --> 00:46:34,950
Really?

410
00:46:39,800 --> 00:46:46,120
Your face is so pale. What is this?

411
00:47:01,780 --> 00:47:04,020
- Forget it.
- Here, too. Here.

412
00:47:05,670 --> 00:47:07,910
Right here, too.

413
00:47:51,150 --> 00:47:57,340
Go in. Aren't you going to go in? Let's go in together.

414
00:48:08,170 --> 00:48:13,630
If we're able to succeed in the Japanese markets, word will get out that sales were successful overseas

415
00:48:13,630 --> 00:48:17,370
and the chances of domestic markets reopening become high.

416
00:48:17,370 --> 00:48:19,630
It'll be good for us even if we can't get into the markets deeply.

417
00:48:19,630 --> 00:48:22,960
Daeseung Company will make the winning move with the taste of our rice wine.

418
00:48:22,960 --> 00:48:27,790
The japanese customers who had tasted the Daeseong Company. cloud liquor distributed in the hotels,

419
00:48:27,790 --> 00:48:31,520
were very favorable, which is a very good omen for hope.

420
00:48:31,520 --> 00:48:35,590
Okay. We have to at least to something.

421
00:48:35,590 --> 00:48:37,940
What do you think, Eun Jo?

422
00:48:37,940 --> 00:48:41,100
I'll go on a business trip to Japan.

423
00:48:41,100 --> 00:48:43,800
I'd like to analyze the local situation myself.

424
00:48:43,800 --> 00:48:46,020
I'll go.

425
00:48:47,860 --> 00:48:48,850
Really?

426
00:48:48,850 --> 00:48:51,330
I'll go with Hyo Seon.

427
00:48:56,350 --> 00:49:01,110
To my knowledge, Hyo Seon wants to turn a new leaf

428
00:49:01,110 --> 00:49:03,680
and I think this business trip will help her.

429
00:49:16,150 --> 00:49:21,840
You said you wouldn't let me rely on you.

430
00:49:23,260 --> 00:49:25,680
Or anyone...

431
00:49:25,680 --> 00:49:28,050
I'm not letting you rely on anyone.

432
00:49:28,650 --> 00:49:33,670
I'm going to show you what you have to do if you don't want to get anything taken from you.

433
00:49:33,670 --> 00:49:37,090
You said Eun Jo didn't take anything from me.

434
00:49:38,190 --> 00:49:43,730
When not only Eun Jo, but anyone, tries to take something from you and attacks,

435
00:49:44,710 --> 00:49:47,690
you need to protect it.

436
00:50:13,110 --> 00:50:15,850
These are the plane tickets and vouchers for the hotel.

437
00:50:15,850 --> 00:50:19,990
I've also included a list of people to meet and their contacts.

438
00:50:19,990 --> 00:50:26,670
He said to sleep early, because you need to leave early in the morning tomorrow.

439
00:50:34,970 --> 00:50:39,870
Excuse me. The president wants to see you.

440
00:50:42,520 --> 00:50:44,790
Excuse me, Mr. Han Jeong Woo.

441
00:50:51,790 --> 00:50:53,920
Why have you packed your things?

442
00:50:53,920 --> 00:50:57,150
Aren't I getting chased out?

443
00:50:58,400 --> 00:51:01,160
I've figured out where Hyo Seon's uncle went.

444
00:51:01,160 --> 00:51:04,790
You'll go with me together, tomorrow.

445
00:51:05,390 --> 00:51:08,130
To...gether?

446
00:51:08,130 --> 00:51:10,280
Leave your belongings and follow me.

447
00:51:13,300 --> 00:51:15,810
You found out where Uncle is?

448
00:51:40,610 --> 00:51:42,290
What?

449
00:51:42,290 --> 00:51:44,050
It's nothing.

450
00:51:45,400 --> 00:51:47,980
Stop looking around and focus on driving.

451
00:51:48,870 --> 00:51:51,360
Yes, I understand.

452
00:52:10,770 --> 00:52:14,600
When I was younger, as someone cut kimchi,

453
00:52:14,600 --> 00:52:18,040
if I ate kimchi like this next to them,

454
00:52:18,040 --> 00:52:23,050
the person cutting the kimchi would slap my hand away.

455
00:52:26,320 --> 00:52:28,090
I'm just saying.

456
00:52:34,000 --> 00:52:35,900
Why aren't you finishing your food?

457
00:52:37,540 --> 00:52:40,970
You and I never had leftovers.

458
00:52:42,380 --> 00:52:47,810
Sit down and finish it all, Noona.

459
00:52:55,560 --> 00:52:57,740
I told you,

460
00:52:57,740 --> 00:53:04,220
wherever you're living and whatever you're doing, I'd find you, and your life...

461
00:53:14,590 --> 00:53:16,940
You're that Han Jeong Woo?

462
00:53:19,940 --> 00:53:25,220
I wondered when you would recognize me. It took you so long.

463
00:53:26,080 --> 00:53:27,810
You're that Jeong Woo?

464
00:53:27,810 --> 00:53:29,430
That's what I said.

465
00:53:35,600 --> 00:53:39,860
You still can't believe it? I am that Jeong Woo.

466
00:53:41,060 --> 00:53:42,390
Why didn't you tell me earlier?

467
00:53:42,390 --> 00:53:46,790
I told you I was waiting until you would recognize me.

468
00:53:46,790 --> 00:53:50,030
I just told you since you really weren't catching on.

469
00:53:57,540 --> 00:54:01,460
If I hadn't told you, then you would've never recognized me, would you?

470
00:54:01,460 --> 00:54:04,850
How could I recognize that this Jeong Woo is the same as that Jeong Woo?

471
00:54:04,850 --> 00:54:08,410
Is your heart fluttering because of how handsome I've become?

472
00:54:09,110 --> 00:54:11,630
If you mess around, I'll hit you.

473
00:54:11,630 --> 00:54:15,610
Hit me. I really want to get hit with those hands of yours.

474
00:54:27,380 --> 00:54:30,590
We were told he had stayed here for sure.

475
00:54:30,590 --> 00:54:32,360
He was here. Did I say he wasn't?

476
00:54:32,360 --> 00:54:37,620
He was here for multiple days, but ran away without even paying his balance!

477
00:54:37,620 --> 00:54:40,020
Did he not tell you where he was going?

478
00:54:40,020 --> 00:54:43,740
Hey. Have you seen someone running away tell you where he'd be going before he left?

479
00:54:43,740 --> 00:54:47,810
How are you related to him? You should pay for his stay instead of him!

480
00:54:56,260 --> 00:54:58,270
He left?

481
00:55:01,690 --> 00:55:04,430
I don't think he'll return.

482
00:55:09,200 --> 00:55:14,470
I heard he bought land with the money he earned from selling the spoiled alcohol,

483
00:55:14,470 --> 00:55:18,190
but it seemed he was scammed in that.

484
00:55:18,190 --> 00:55:21,710
I think he ran away because he was so ashamed.

485
00:55:21,710 --> 00:55:26,080
I'm waiting for someone to contact me,

486
00:55:26,080 --> 00:55:30,170
so don't go anywhere far and just wait a bit there.

487
00:55:44,640 --> 00:55:48,360
Honey, Joon Soo is excited about going on a trip with you. He's waiting.

488
00:55:48,360 --> 00:55:50,530
Okay, sure.

489
00:55:54,190 --> 00:55:57,680
Are you feeling sick somewhere?

490
00:55:57,680 --> 00:56:01,190
No... I'm okay.

491
00:56:01,190 --> 00:56:04,700
You haven't even been able to rest these days because you've got so much on your plate.

492
00:56:04,700 --> 00:56:08,870
You should rest a bit for now. Play with Joon Soo next time.

493
00:56:08,870 --> 00:56:12,340
Spending time with my son is resting.

494
00:56:15,060 --> 00:56:17,030
Will you really be okay?

495
00:56:17,030 --> 00:56:19,560
I told you I'm fine.

496
00:56:24,410 --> 00:56:25,730
Daddy!

497
00:56:25,730 --> 00:56:29,770
My little Joon Soo.

498
00:56:34,500 --> 00:56:37,640
Okay, let's go!

499
00:56:39,820 --> 00:56:43,670
Japan

500
00:56:51,450 --> 00:56:53,080
Oppa,

501
00:56:54,300 --> 00:56:57,080
do you know how to speak Japanese?

502
00:56:58,590 --> 00:57:01,410
I don't know how to speak a single word.

503
00:57:01,410 --> 00:57:06,610
It's okay. They're distinguished representatives from the liquor marketing in Japan.

504
00:57:06,610 --> 00:57:10,370
They studied Korean because they're fans of Korean dramas.

505
00:57:19,340 --> 00:57:22,040
Hello.

506
00:57:47,650 --> 00:57:50,850
- It's delicious.
- Super good.

507
00:57:50,850 --> 00:57:54,150
Even Hallyu actors drink this alcohol.

508
00:57:54,960 --> 00:57:59,850
In Korea, we can guarantee that there is no other that compares to the taste of our rice wines.

509
00:57:59,850 --> 00:58:03,070
Though we can't compare to the size of larger corporations,

510
00:58:03,070 --> 00:58:07,020
the taste of our alcohols is shaking up the Korean markets.

511
00:58:07,720 --> 00:58:10,690
I know this person.

512
00:58:10,690 --> 00:58:16,950
We saw her commercial on YouTube.

513
00:58:17,600 --> 00:58:20,700
You're very beautiful.

514
00:58:20,700 --> 00:58:22,430
Thank you.

515
00:58:22,430 --> 00:58:27,070
My son is usually very quiet, but he saw your video

516
00:58:27,130 --> 00:58:31,600
and talks to be about you a lot,

517
00:58:31,600 --> 00:58:33,610
saying you're very pretty.

518
00:58:34,700 --> 00:58:35,890
I see.

519
00:58:35,890 --> 00:58:39,510
I know this isn't very courteous, but I'd like to invite you to my house

520
00:58:39,510 --> 00:58:41,930
before you leave.

521
00:58:41,930 --> 00:58:46,880
I think my son would be impressed.

522
00:58:57,060 --> 00:58:59,960
We will gratefully accept your invitation.

523
00:59:00,930 --> 00:59:02,830
Thank you.

524
00:59:02,830 --> 00:59:04,890
Thank you.

525
00:59:34,350 --> 00:59:38,430
- What is it?
- Take it. It's yours.

526
00:59:41,080 --> 00:59:43,430
I saved up everything,

527
00:59:44,300 --> 00:59:48,000
without taking a single cent, from what I earned in the Marines.

528
00:59:48,000 --> 00:59:52,630
It's not a lot, but it's my entire life's savings.

529
01:00:01,560 --> 01:00:04,220
Why are you giving this to me?

530
01:00:05,340 --> 01:00:07,800
I saved it up to give it to you.

531
01:00:08,520 --> 01:00:13,040
Exactly. Why did you save it up for me?

532
01:00:14,060 --> 01:00:19,130
This woman.. Are you asking because you really don't know?

533
01:00:20,930 --> 01:00:26,200
Who else would I give my first earnings to?

534
01:00:31,240 --> 01:00:35,730
How is Mr. Jang doing?

535
01:00:39,130 --> 01:00:44,520
Never mind, forget it. Don't answer. I'm not curious.

536
01:00:49,340 --> 01:00:51,230
I don't know either.

537
01:00:52,470 --> 01:00:57,980
I... lived alone ever since I was 16.

538
01:00:59,510 --> 01:01:02,360
To be exact, I wasn't alone.

539
01:01:03,400 --> 01:01:05,910
I lived with you.

540
01:01:07,480 --> 01:01:12,140
What about baseball? Did you quit baseball?

541
01:01:16,620 --> 01:01:20,810
I lived with you.

542
01:01:29,780 --> 01:01:31,820
Stop messing around.

543
01:01:32,610 --> 01:01:34,140
Okay.

544
01:01:37,820 --> 01:01:40,500
I'll take this for now.

545
01:01:40,500 --> 01:01:41,960
Really?

546
01:01:41,960 --> 01:01:47,030
I'll give it to you when you get married, along with interest or some more funds.

547
01:01:55,850 --> 01:01:57,700
Hello?

548
01:02:04,730 --> 01:02:06,200
Oppa.

549
01:02:08,180 --> 01:02:09,940
Oppa.

550
01:02:11,980 --> 01:02:13,610
Oppa!

551
01:02:15,560 --> 01:02:17,110
What is it?

552
01:02:19,100 --> 01:02:20,880
Oppa...

553
01:02:23,330 --> 01:02:25,190
Oppa...

554
01:02:28,380 --> 01:02:30,850
Dad...

555
01:02:30,850 --> 01:02:32,700
What about the president?

556
01:02:34,690 --> 01:02:40,190
Dad... fainted.

557
01:02:44,500 --> 01:02:51,760
Dad fainted after he went to go play with Joon Soo.

558
01:03:02,720 --> 01:03:09,780
♫ Like this for another day, month or year
♫

559
01:03:09,780 --> 01:03:14,640
♫ I don't mind even if I am hurt. ♫

560
01:03:14,640 --> 01:03:17,200
Are you treating me like a crazy woman right now, Granny?

561
01:03:17,220 --> 01:03:19,750
With Father...

562
01:03:21,150 --> 01:03:25,400
- Are you okay?
- My heart is beating quickly.

563
01:03:26,290 --> 01:03:29,350
If you treat Hyo Seon poorly, I'll kill you with my own hands.

564
01:03:29,350 --> 01:03:32,640
You can just pretend I'm not here.

565
01:03:33,430 --> 01:03:34,810
Let go! Let go!

566
01:03:34,810 --> 01:03:37,600
Until where are you going to run? I'll run for you.

567
01:03:37,600 --> 01:03:44,780
♫ Can't you hear my voice? ♫
